## Estimated Hours for Learning Activities

I spent approximately **4 hours** working on this topic during the week. This included installing LocalWP, creating a local WordPress website, exploring the WordPress dashboard, and learning how to manage plugins and website content.

## Content Insights

Setting up a local WordPress environment provided a valuable introduction to the process of developing dynamic websites safely before publishing them online. I learned that LocalWP automatically configures important components such as PHP, MySQL, and the web server, making the setup process much easier for beginners.

I also gained a deeper understanding of how WordPress functions as a content management system (CMS). Unlike static websites, WordPress stores content in a database and dynamically generates web pages. Through this practical experience, I became more confident in managing WordPress sites and troubleshooting local development issues.
